0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MAY 2, 2007\r\rMayor Bozajian called the meeting to order at 7:31 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Bozajian, Mayor pro Tem Maurer, Councilmembers Groveman, Washburn, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Colantuono, Coroalles, Parker, Rubin, Seferian, Steller, Tamuri.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Don Franken.\r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r\r Councilmember Wolfson moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Bozajian presented a proclamation to Sparky Cohen, Building Official, declaring �Building Safety Week� in the City of Calabasas. Mayor Bozajian presented a plaque to Don Franken in recognition of his work on the MethodFest 2007. Councilmember Washburn announced an open audition that will be held at Pierce College for �Carousel�. Mayor Bozajian announced that three events will be occurring: the Calabasas Arts Festival on May 5 and 6, 2007; the Annual Summer Pops Concert on May 20, 2007; and the Historical Society�s Annual BBQ on June 10, 2007.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r No indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r \rAdoption of Ordinance No. 2007-234, amending Section 17.14.020 of the Calabasas Municipal Code \u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015to conditionally allow medical service uses in the Commercial-Old Town Zoning District.\r \rAdoption of Ordinance No. 2007-235, approving ZCH-007-001 for the correction of mapping errors for a General Plan Land Use Map designation boundary line and a Zoning Designation boundary line to be consistent with a previous action taken by the City Council, and which will result in no net reduction in open space lands.\r\r Recommendation to award a professional services agreement to Telecommunications Management Corporation for cable consulting services in an amount not to exceed $15,000.\r \rRecommendation to approve the appointment of Melissa Olin by Councilmember Wolfson to the Environmental Commission, term ending March 2009.\r\rRecommendation to approve the appointment of Councilmember Wolfson as a Boardmember to the Economic Alliance of the San Fernando Valley Board of Directors.\r\rRecommendation to authorize staff to reduce the Performance Security Grading Bond (SU5006070) by 50% for New Millennium Homes, One Tract 35596: 16-25.\r\rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve Consent Items # 2, 3, 4, 7, 8 and 9. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\rNEW BUSINESS\r \rDiscussion regarding extension of the Rental Assistance Program.\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rReva Isaacman, President of the Calabasas Village Homeowners Association, spoke in support of extending the Rental Assistance Program. Charles Barkley, Calabasas, thanked the City Council for their support of the Rental Assistance Program.\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn to extend the Rental Assistance Program with an increase to the subsidy and program amount. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUpdate on the Rental Registration Program\r\rMaureen Tamuri, Community Development Director, presented the staff report.\r\rFalgurri Trieu, Calabasas, spoke in support of instituting rent control in the City. Alex Winborn, Manager, Archstone Calabasas, provided answers to inquiries from the City Council. \r\rThere was no action taken.\r\r The following items were heard out of order of the agenda:\r\r Approval of the minutes for the April 18, 2007 City Council meeting. \r\rMayor pro Tem Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn, to approve Consent Item #1 with a revision to the Announcements/Introductions section in the minutes. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\r5. Recommendation from the Parks, Recreation and Education Commission to award Community Service Grants for the�third funding cycle of FY 06/07 as identified in the staff report.\r\rMayor pro Tem Maurer RECUSED herself from Item #5. Following discussion, Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to approve the recommendation to award Community Service Grants. MOTION CARRIED 4/0 with Mayor pro Tem Maurer�s RECUSAL.\r\r6. Recommendation to accept the Annual Citywide Rubberized Overlay Project by Security Paving Inc. Specification No. 05-06-04; and to direct the City Clerk to file for the Notice of Completion.\r\rFollowing discussion, Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to accept the Annual Citywide Rubberized Overlay Project. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\rCheck Register for the period of April 11, 2007 to April 19, 2007.\r\rThere was no action taken.\r\rDiscussion of participation in All-America City Award Competition.\r\rJohn Bingham, Senior Management Analyst, presented the staff report.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff for participation in the All-America City Award Competition.\r\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS\r\r Councilmember Washburn spoke regarding the Stream to Sea event that occurred at Headwaters Corners.\r\rRECESSED TO FRIENDS OF THE ARTS IN CALABASAS BOARD OF DIRECTORS MEETING\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT\r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated that he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\r\r The City Council requested that a discussion regarding water quality and watershed issues be placed on a future agenda.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:05 p.m. \r\r\r\r_____